  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1147 PM CDT MON SEP 14 2026\n\nPersistent upper-level ridging remains the main story for this\nforecast period, with the ridge centered over Tennessee. This\npattern will effectively suppress rain chances through Friday,\nkeeping afternoon PoPs under 10%. Under the influence of high\npressure, high temperatures will hold in the low-to-upper 90s\nthrough the upcoming weekend. Although actual temperatures will\nbe hot, lower dew points within this drier airmass should keep\nheat indices in the 101-104 range, remaining below advisory\nthresholds.\n\nBy the weekend, the upper-level pattern is expected to shift as\nan upper low tracks from the Atlantic into the Gulf around the\nperiphery of the ridge. While model guidance shows uncertainty\nregarding the exact placement and intensity of this feature, any\nmoisture returning to the Gulf should weaken the ridge and bring\nhigher rain chances for the weekend.\n\n16",
